// RunState is the durable workflow state used by the Temporal Run entrypoint.
// It allows the workflow to continue-as-new while carrying only the minimal
// required subset of previously produced outputs for the remaining steps.
// WorkloadIdentity describes who a run acts as.
//
// A running workload has two identities at once, and both matter. It is a
// specific workload (this workflow, this run, this step) and it is acting on
// behalf of whoever asked for the work. Downstream systems need both to make an
// authorization decision: "the nightly-reconcile workflow" and "started by the
// deploy pipeline" answer different questions, and a system granting access
// usually cares about the pair.
//
// This is carried through the run so that every step knows what it is acting as,
// and so an assertion presented to an external system states something true
// rather than something assumed. It holds identity, never credentials: it is
// persisted in workflow history, which is durable and broadly readable, so
